{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["וְנָתַנּוּ — dagged [doubbling], like ונתננו, meaning 'is given' — וְנָתַנְנוּ; and likewise מצרים נתנו יד — like נתננו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The comment reads as ellipsis: the dagged form ונתנו is functionally equivalent to the fuller ונתננו; the second example, מצרים נתנו יד, is cited as another instance where a dagged nun-form parallels the undagged."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:12.416544038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}